    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/assistant-dean-of-academic-advising": {
      "title": "Assistant Dean of Academic Advising -",
      "description": "Assistant Dean of Academic Advising - University website My Profile Kiosk mode Join our team Assistant Dean of Academic Advising Assistant Dean of Academic Advising 493046 256 - Ctr For Advising/Retention Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time On-site $120,000 - $125,000 Add to favorites View favorites Overview The Assistant Dean of Academic Advising provides strategic leadership for academic advising at Salem State University. Reporting to the Assistant Vice President for the Center for Academic Excellence, the Assistant Dean leads the development, implementation, assessment, and continuous improvement of a shared advising model that promotes student success, persistence, and on-time degree completion. The Assistant Dean collaborates with colleagues across the Student Success and Academic Affairs divisions, working with deans, faculty, and professional staff to strengthen advising practices, enhance the student experience, and advance institutional goals related to retention and graduation. The position serves as the institution's lead administrator for advising strategy, assessment, policy development, advisor training, and advising technologies. What you do at Salem State University matters. As a staff member, you'll be part of an institution that is a proud Hispanic-Serving Institution and that serves one of the most diverse student bodies in Massachusetts. We believe in building a workplace culture that mirrors our values: inclusive, equitable and driven by a genuine desire to help people succeed. You'll find professional development opportunities, a supportive team environment and work that connects directly to our students' futures. Required Qualifications Master’s degree Eight years of progressively responsible experience in academic advising, student success, retention, or related higher education administration Experience supervising professional staff Experience using data to make decisions Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree Experience with student success platforms (e.g. EAB Navigate 360) Experience supervising employees in a unionized environment Experience with shared advising models Experience collaborating with faculty and academic leadership Experience with advisor training Demonstrated experience successfully leading cross-functional teams Demonstrated commitment to access, equity, and student success Working Location This is an onsite position in Salem, MA with on-campus, in-person responsibilities, which may require occasional/frequent/regular work on evenings and weekends. Application Instructions Please apply online and attach  resume and cover letter. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. This position is not eligible for H1B visa sponsorship. EEO Statement The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. ADA Statement Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. For accommodation information or requests please email eo-hr@salemstate.edu . Recruitment Agencies Salem State University does not partner with or accept candidates from outside staffing agencies. All hiring is managed directly by our internal Talent Acquisition team. Apply now First Name (required) 2b1db0a2 Last Name (required) 3c0d593b Email (required) 876e37f1 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Adjunct Faculty Day, Healthcare Studies, AY 2025-2026 493102 723 - Healthcare Studies Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Adjunct Faculty Evening - Continuing Education, English, AY 2026-2027 493089 163 - English Faculty: Adjunct, Staff: Temporary/Contract Part-Time Faculty: History, (Early American and Public History), Full-Time, Temporary 493082 190 - History Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Non-Tenure-Track (Temp) Director of Academic Operations 493076 101 - Academic Affairs/ OVP Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Field Placement and First-Year Advising Coordinator 493038 234 - Psychology Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Adjunct Faculty Day, World Lang & Cultures and Education, AY 2026-2027 493079 177 - World Languages / Cultures Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) bb6b655e Last Name (required) 4b21fdc6 Email (required) 7bcfb05b Job Alert 596e5571 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 256 - Ctr For Advising/Retention 256 - Ctr For Advising/Retention Categories Staff: Administrator/Professional Staff: Administrator/Professional Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Working location On-site On-site Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Apply Now First Name (required) 1a4b1fc4 Last Name (required) bffe0acb Email (required) 75c2b2c5 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. You can view our university policies here . Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Technical and functional cookies are required for the Website to work. These include, for example, session management, Website security, shopping cart, lan