    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/director-of-academic-operations": {
      "title": "Director of Academic Operations -",
      "description": "Director of Academic Operations - University website My Profile Kiosk mode Join our team Director of Academic Operations Director of Academic Operations 493076 101 - Academic Affairs/ OVP Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time On-site $95,000 - $105,000 Add to favorites View favorites Overview Under the direction of the Provost and Academic Vice President, the Director of Academic Operations provides strategic and operational leadership for core administrative functions within the Division of Academic Affairs. The Director leads cross-functional projects, develops and implements divisional operating systems, advises academic leadership on budgetary, facilities, and other administrative matters, and ensures that Academic Affairs operations are aligned with institutional priorities, including the university’s strategic plan. The position exercises independent judgment in coordinating complex initiatives, recommending process improvements, managing divisional workflows, and representing the Provost’s Office with internal and external stakeholders. The Director advances this work through shared administrative support, cross-functional leadership, and established Academic Affairs processes. The Director also leads annual planning and execution for Academic Convocation (September) and Commencement (May). Salem State University is more than a workplace. It's a community with purpose. As the Commonwealth's Civic Engagement University, we're committed to building real, reciprocal relationships with the communities around us, and that starts with the people who work here. We're also a proud Hispanic-Serving Institution dedicated to serving all students, and that same commitment to access and equity extends to how we support our staff. Your work here directly contributes to student success and the vitality of the greater Salem community. We invest in our people the same way we invest in our students: with intention, respect and a genuine interest in your growth. Required Qualifications Master’s degree in higher education administration, business, or a relevant field. Minimum of five years of progressively responsible administrative experience in higher education, with demonstrated knowledge of the principles, practices, and procedures of higher education. Demonstrated experience in budget planning and management, financial analysis, and process improvement with the capacity to implement independently as appropriate. Demonstrated experience leading cross-functional projects or operational portfolios. Knowledge of necessary software applications, including advanced Microsoft Excel functions, Word, PowerPoint, Outlook, Teams, and PeopleSoft, with the ability to perform PeopleSoft inquiries related to job duties. Preferred Qualifications Seven or more years of progressively responsible administrative experience in higher education, with demonstrated knowledge of the principles, practices, and procedures of higher education. Superior communication skills at all levels of the organization, including students, faculty, staff, and senior administrators, including demonstrated excellence in written communication. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously and reprioritize as needed. Demonstrated ability to exercise sound judgment, professionalism, patience, diplomacy, and discretion in complex or time-sensitive situations. Working Location This is an onsite position in Salem, MA with on-campus, in-person responsibilities, which may require occasional work on evenings and weekends. Application Instructions Please apply online and attach resume and cover letter. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. This position is not eligible for H1B visa sponsorship. EEO Statement The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. ADA Statement Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. For accommodation information or requests please email eo-hr@salemstate.edu . Recruitment Agencies Salem State University does not partner with or accept candidates from outside staffing agencies. All hiring is managed directly by our internal Talent Acquisition team. Apply now First Name (required) 88191b56 Last Name (required) a67a0bff Email (required) 04fc3428 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Adjunct Faculty Day, Healthcare Studies, AY 2025-2026 493102 723 - Healthcare Studies Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Adjunct Faculty Evening - Continuing Education, English, AY 2026-2027 493089 163 - English Faculty: Adjunct, Staff: Temporary/Contract Part-Time Assistant Dean of Academic Advising 493046 256 - Ctr For Advising/Retention Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Faculty: History, (Early American and Public History), Full-Time, Temporary 493082 190 - History Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Non-Tenure-Track (Temp) Field Placement and First-Year Advising Coordinator 493038 234 - Psychology Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Adjunct Faculty Day, World Lang & Cultures and Education, AY 2026-2027 493079 177 - World Languages / Cultures Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) ebd8491c Last Name (required) 917e82f5 Email (required) 30482f9c Job Alert 79c5d15c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 101 - Academic Affairs/ OVP 101 - Academic Affairs/ OVP Categories Staff