    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/field-placement-and-first-year-advising-coordinator": {
      "title": "Field Placement and First-Year Advising Coordinator -",
      "description": "Field Placement and First-Year Advising Coordinator - University website My Profile Kiosk mode Join our team Field Placement and First-Year Advising Coordinator Field Placement and First-Year Advising Coordinator 493038 234 - Psychology Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time On-site $68,000 - $73,000 Add to favorites View favorites Overv iew The psychology department is searching for a Field Placement and First-Year Advising Coordinator. This position will serve as the professional advisor to all first-year undergraduate students majoring in Psychology, which includes academic advising, reviewing major/minor requirements, and referring students to appropriate campus resources as needed. This position will also serve both undergraduate and graduate program needs with respect to all field placements, internships, and practica. The Field Placement and First-Year Advising Coordinator will work closely with Graduate Program Coordinators in Behavior Analysis, Industrial/Organizational Psychology, and Counseling and Psychological Services to manage possible and existing sites, track students’ supervision hours, and verify licensure of participating supervisors. Applicants with BCBA certification are encouraged to apply; however, certification is not required for this position. The psychology department is home to a popular undergraduate major and to master’s degree programs in behavior analysis, counseling, and industrial/organizational psychology. This position is a full-time, 12-month position with an on-site work schedule. At Salem State University, every role on campus plays a part in something meaningful. As a proud Hispanic-Serving Institution, we've built a culture that reflects the diversity of the students and communities we serve, and we bring that same spirit to our workplace. You'll find colleagues who are collaborative, students who are motivated and a mission you can stand behind. Whether you're just starting your career or bringing years of experience, Salem State is a place where your contributions count. Required Qualifications • Master’s degree in psychology or a related field • Two to three years of relevant experience • Experience managing relationships between organizations • Excellent organizational skills and written communication skills • Proficient in Learning Management Systems and Microsoft Office Suite Preferred Qualifications • Board Certified Behavior Analyst (BCBA) • Knowledge of Behavior Analysis Certification Board (BACB) requirements • Experience supervising, mentoring, or advising students or other individuals • Experience in higher education Working Location This is an onsite position in Salem, MA with on-campus, in-person responsibilities, which may require occasional work on evenings and weekends. Application Instructions Please apply online and attach resume and cover letter. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. This position is not eligible for H1B visa sponsorship. EEO Statement The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. ADA Statement Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. For accommodation information or requests please email eo-hr@salemstate.edu . Recruitment Agencies Salem State University does not partner with or accept candidates from outside staffing agencies. All hiring is managed directly by our internal Talent Acquisition team. Apply now First Name (required) 54cc46b1 Last Name (required) c17d901f Email (required) 9ace926c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Adjunc