    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/adjunct-faculty-day-world-lang-cultures-and-education-ay-2026-2027": {
      "title": "Join our team",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty Day, World Lang & Cultures and Education, AY 2026-2027 - University website My Profile Kiosk mode Join our team Adjunct Faculty Day, World Lang & Cultures and Education, AY 2026-2027 Adjunct Faculty Day, World Lang & Cultures and Education, AY 2026-2027 493079 177 - World Languages / Cultures Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Hybrid $1,000 - $2,253.60 per Semester Hour Credit of Instruction Add to favorites View favorites Salem State University invites applications for a temporary Adjunct Professor of Spanish Education with a joint appointment in the Department of World Languages and Cultures and the McKeown School of Education for spring 2027. This position plays a central leadership role in the university’s Spanish teacher licensure programs. The candidate will teach Spanish teacher licensure courses for the 4+1 BA/MEd with Initial Licensure and the Master of Arts in Teaching (MAT) in Spanish. These programs are jointly supported by the Department of World Languages and Cultures and the McKeown School of Education. Teaching Responsibilities Teaching responsibilities will be distributed across the two units and will focus primarily on licensure-related coursework, including but not limited to: • Spanish Methods I and II courses with integrated, co-requisite field experiences • Student teaching seminar and practicum • Advanced-track courses such as Action Research and Clinical sequences Service & Professional Engagement The candidate will be expected to: • Engage in service activities in both the Department of World Languages and Cultures and the McKeown School of Education • Collaborate across disciplines to align licensure curricula, assessment practices, and clinical expectations • Participate actively in state, regional, and national professional organizations related to world language education Working Location: This is an onsite position in Salem, MA with some on-campus, in-person responsibilities. Application Instructions: Please apply online and attach CV, cover letter, and official transcripts. To ensure you are assigned the highest eligible rank, you should provide the total sum of credits you have taught at the college/university level.  This information can be added to your CV, cover letter, or a separate document. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. This position is not eligible for H1B visa sponsorship. EEO Statement: The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Apply now First Name (required) 8dc511b0 Last Name (required) f557f7e6 Email (required) d1da23c9 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Adjunct Faculty Day, Healthcare Studies, AY 2025-2026 493102 723 - Healthcare Studies Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Adjunct Faculty Evening - Continuing Education, English, AY 2026-2027 493089 163 - English Faculty: Adjunct, Staff: Temporary/Contract Part-Time Assistant Dean of Academic Advising 493046 256 - Ctr For Advising/Retention Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Faculty: History, (Early American and Public History), Full-Time, Temporary 493082 190 - History Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Non-Tenure-Track (Temp) Director of Academic Operations 493076 101 - Academic Affairs/ OVP Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Field Placement and First-Year Advising Coordinator 493038 234 - Psychology Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 15c21a87 Last Name (required) e17e4768 Email (required) c1c01365 Job Alert 9565221d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and