    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/faculty-criminal-justice-security-management-full-time-tenure-track": {
      "title": "Faculty, Criminal Justice (Security Management), Full-Time, Tenure-Track -",
      "description": "Faculty, Criminal Justice (Security Management), Full-Time, Tenure-Track - University website My Profile Kiosk mode Join our team Faculty, Criminal Justice (Security Management), Full-Time, Tenure-Track Faculty, Criminal Justice (Security Management), Full-Time, Tenure-Track 492961 236 - Criminal Justice Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track On-site $90,000-$95,000 (for the rank of assistant professor) Add to favorites View favorites Overview The Criminal Justice Department seeks a dynamic and engaged educator for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position beginning in Fall 2027. This faculty member specializes in Security Studies will possess the demonstrated ability to teach courses in homeland security, terrorism, and emergency management. The successful candidate will contribute to a vibrant academic community by teaching a range of foundational undergraduate courses such as criminal justice ethics, criminal law, statistics, research methods, theory, policing, courts, corrections, and global crime and justice, as well as courses within the graduate program. The ideal candidate will bring a commitment to student success, interdisciplinary collaboration, and innovative approaches to teaching, learning, and mentoring. At Salem State University, we are deeply committed to academic excellence and the transformative power of higher education. We pride ourselves in providing first-rate classroom experiences and supervising intensive learning opportunities such as research and internships. As a faculty member, you will play a vital role in shaping the learning and growth of our students, many of whom are the first in their families to attend college. We value collegiality, collaboration and a dedication to student success. Join us in a community that prioritizes civic engagement and continuous improvement, where your contributions will help build a socially just world and inspire the next generation of scholars. Duties and Responsibilities Candidates are required to perform duties in accordance with the MSCA contract . Duties include teaching, advising, scholarship and contributions to continuously improve the department and university. The standard teaching load is 12 credit hours per semester. The position is subject to available funding. Required Qualifications PhD in criminal justice or closely related field, or ABD with doctorate conferred by August 2027. Experience in and the demonstrated ability to teach in areas of Security Studies, including Homeland Security, Terrorism, and Emergency Management. Experience in and the demonstrated ability to teach a variety of core courses within the undergraduate program such as criminal justice ethics, criminal law, statistics, theories, research methods, policing, courts, corrections and global crime and justice, as well as the graduate program in criminal justice. Evidence of successful teaching experience at the college/university level. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching face-to-face, hybrid, and online courses. Experience in distance learning and instructional technologies. Experience serving as role a model and mentor for students from a variety of backgrounds and experiences. Evidence of scholarly research in Security Management and/or Criminal Justice issues. As a Hispanic and Minority Serving Institution (HSI/MSI), Salem State University seeks to enrich the faculty/librarian ranks by actively encouraging candidates body of scholarly work addresses issues regarding the welfare and representation of historically under-served communities in our region. Candidates should present documented activities in appropriately aligned teaching, scholarship/research, and service, including community-based endeavors. Working Location This is an onsite position in Salem, MA with on-campus, in-person responsibilities. Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. For accommodation information or requests please email eo-hr@salemstate.edu . Application Instructions Please apply online and attach CV, cover letter, and unofficial transcripts. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. All applicants are encouraged to apply; however, Salem State University cannot guarantee that it will sponsor visas for individuals who are not otherwise authorized to work in the United States. EEO Statement The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. ADA Statement Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. For accommodation information or requests please email eo-hr@salemstate.edu . Recruitment Agencies Salem State University does not partner with or accept candidates from outside staffing agencies. All hiring is managed directly by our internal Talent Acquisition team. Apply now First Name (required) 1c46c587 Last Name (required) dfca87cb Email (required) b779880d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Adjunct Faculty Day, Healthcare Studies, AY 2025-2026 493102 723 - Healthcare Studies Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Adjunct Faculty Evening - Continuing Education, English, AY 2026-2027 493089 163 - English Faculty: Adjunct, Staff: Temporary/Contract Part-Time Assistant Dean of Academic Advising 493046 256 - Ctr For Advising/Retention Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Faculty: History, (Early American and Public History), Full-Time, Temporary 493082 190 - History Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Non-Tenure-Track (Temp) Director of Academic Ope