    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/faculty-childhood-education-special-education-full-time-tenure-track": {
      "title": "Faculty: Childhood Education (Special Education), Full-Time, Tenure-Track -",
      "description": "Faculty: Childhood Education (Special Education), Full-Time, Tenure-Track - University website My Profile Kiosk mode Join our team Faculty: Childhood Education (Special Education), Full-Time, Tenure-Track Faculty: Childhood Education (Special Education), Full-Time, Tenure-Track 492981 443 - Childhood Education and Care Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track On-site $80,000 - $85,000 (for the rank of assistant professor) Add to favorites View favorites Overview Salem State University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position in Special Education beginning in Fall 2027. The successful candidate will contribute to a dynamic educator preparation program committed to inclusive practices, equity, and strong partnerships with schools and communities. Salem State University offers an environment where academic excellence and student success are paramount. We seek faculty who are passionate about educating a diverse student body of learners and leaders and who thrive in a collegial and collaborative setting. As an Hispanic and Minority Serving institution, we are dedicated to civic engagement and the success of first-generation college students, we value initiative, continuous improvement and accountability. Join our community, where your scholarship and teaching will have a lasting impact on both the university and the greater world. Duties and Responsibilities Candidates are required to perform duties in accordance with the MSCA contract. Duties include teaching, advising, scholarship and contributions to continuously improve the department and university. The standard teaching load is 12 credit hours per semester. The position is subject to available funding. Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Special Education in multiple modalities Supervise teacher candidates in pre-practicum and/or practicum field experiences Develop and maintain partnerships with local schools and districts to support practicum experiences and collaborative initiatives Participate in program development, accreditation processes Required Qualifications Earned doctoral degree in Special Education or a closely related field (conferred by August 1, 2027) Professional experience as a Special Education teacher Demonstrated commitment to inclusive instructional practices in educational settings and culturally responsive practices A scholarly agenda Expertise in one or more of the following areas: Evidence-based instructional practices, materials, and methods for teaching students with moderate disabilities Literacy instruction for students with disabilities Diagnostic and educational assessment for students with disabilities Development, interpretation, and implementation of Individualized Education Programs (IEPs) Autism spectrum disorder, including school-based and home-based interventions, collaboration with families, and advocacy for students with autism Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching in higher education Experience with online asynchronous or hybrid instruction and learning management systems, such as Canvas Strong organizational and written and communication skills Salem State University seeks faculty and librarians whose teaching, scholarship, and service will contribute to student success, academic excellence, and the university’s public mission. We welcome candidates with demonstrated ability to work effectively with students from varied backgrounds and to support an inclusive learning environment. Applicants may describe relevant accomplishments in teaching, scholarship/research, service, and community-engaged work Working Location This is an onsite position in Salem, MA with on-campus, in-person responsibilities. Application Instructions Please apply online and attach CV, cover letter, and unofficial transcripts. Application review will commence in September. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. All applicants are encouraged to apply; however, Salem State University cannot guarantee that it will sponsor visas for individuals who are not otherwise authorized to work in the United States. EEO Statement The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. ADA Statement Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. For accommodation information or requests please email eo-hr@salemstate.edu . Recruitment Agencies Salem State University does not partner with or accept candidates from outside staffing agencies. All hiring is managed directly by our internal Talent Acquisition team. Apply now First Name (required) d9e9d030 Last Name (required) b78c1b54 Email (required) c31be260 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Adjunct Faculty Day, Healthcare Studies, AY 2025-2026 493102 723 - Healthcare Studies Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Adjunct Faculty Evening - Continuing Education, English, AY 2026-2027 493089 163 - English Faculty: Adjunct, Staff: Temporary/Contract Part-Time Assistant Dean of Academic Advising 493046 256 - Ctr For Advising/Retention Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Faculty: History, (Early American and Public History), Full-Time, Temporary 493082 190 - History Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Non-Tenure-Track (Temp) Director of Academic Operations 493076 101 - Academic Affairs/ OVP Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Field Placement and First-Year Advising Coordinator 493038 234 - Psychology Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) fc6eb886 Last Name (required) abd7e8dc Email (required) b39dc252 Job Alert f30f011a 