    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/corporate-and-foundation-relations-assistant": {
      "title": "Corporate and Foundation Relations Assistant -",
      "description": "Corporate and Foundation Relations Assistant - University website My Profile Kiosk mode Join our team Corporate and Foundation Relations Assistant Corporate and Foundation Relations Assistant 493004 193 - Advancement Office Of VP Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Hybrid $59,000 - $64,000 Add to favorites View favorites Overview The corporate and foundation (C&F) relations assistant works under the direction of the associate director of C&F relations and is responsible for the identification, discovery, qualification, cultivation, solicitation and stewardship of a portfolio of corporate and foundation prospects that can, or already do, support Salem State University through grants, sponsorships, and/or annual gifts. The C&F Assistant interacts with the advancement team, university administrators, faculty, staff and volunteers as appropriate. Some early morning, evening, and weekend work may be requested by the supervisor. Salem State University is a place where your career can flourish. We embrace and celebrate the uniqueness of every employee, creating an inclusive and supportive environment where you can do your best work. Our commitment to civic engagement ensures that your contributions will positively impact both the university and the community. As an emerging Hispanic and minority-serving institution, we are dedicated to fostering diversity and championing social justice. Join us and be part of a transformative community that enriches lives across the Commonwealth. Duties and Responsibilities Writing or editing funding proposals, grant applications, solicitation letters, impact/grant/ sponsorship reports fulfillment and similar documents. Establishing and maintaining relationships with business and organization donors/prospects through in-person and virtual visits, events and correspondence to advance the donor relationship. Researching and identifying new C&F funding sources to support current university priorities. Helping the C&F team meet its annual fundraising goals through active donor solicitation and follow-up. Supporting outreach to corporate sponsorships in coordination with the Associate Director, Engagement events. Managing tracking system for ensuring timely follow through with reporting, proposal deadlines and reporting out pipeline of activity. Managing C&F donor stewardship reporting for donors in portfolio. Recording contact reports and proposal information in a timely manner and in accordance with Salem State prospect management procedures. Working cross-departmentally with on-campus academic and faculty partners in support of documentation sourcing, funder portal management and information submissions (reports, surveys, data collection, etc.). Utilizing the current library of grant development materials. Works a part of the C&F team with the associate director and coordinator. Assist when needed with student staff. Other special projects as assigned. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Two or more years of relevant work experience Superior written and oral communication skills, with exceptional attention to detail and the ability to articulate a compelling case for philanthropic support Demonstrated project management skills Experience and ability to work both collaboratively and independently Proficiency in Windows/Microsoft Office computer applications Preferred Qualifications Experience with corporate and foundation fundraising and/or higher education Thorough understanding of the value of public higher education and ability to articulate that understanding Fundraising experience Proven ability to work in a fast-paced, deadline driven, goal-oriented environment Demonstrated ability to manage complex projects Experience with fundraising and donor management software, preferably Raiser's Edge Working Location This is a hybrid position in Salem, MA with weekly on-campus, in-person responsibilities, which may require occasional work on evenings and weekends. Application Instructions Please apply online and attach resume and cover letter. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. This position is not eligible for H1B visa sponsorship. EEO Statement The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. ADA Statement Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. For accommodation information or requests please email eo-hr@salemstate.edu . Recruitment Agencies Salem State University does not partner with or accept candidates from outside staffing agencies. All hiring is managed directly by our internal Talent Acquisition team. Apply now First Name (required) f083e2ab Last Name (required) 7fbd0004 Email (required) 1594c348 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Adjunct Faculty Day, Healthcare Studies, AY 2025-2026 493102 723 - Healthcare Studies Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Adjunct Faculty Evening - Continuing Education, English, AY 2026-2027 493089 163 - English Faculty: Adjunct, Staff: Temporary/Contract Part-Time Assistant Dean of Academic Advising 493046 256 - Ctr For Advising/Retention Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Faculty: History, (Early American and Public History), Full-Time, Temporary 493082 190 - History Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Non-Tenure-Track (Temp) Director of Academic Operations 493076 101 - Academic Affairs/ OVP Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Field Placement and First-Year Advising Coordinator 493038 234 - Psychology Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 59ae3af8 