    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/athletic-trainer": {
      "title": "Join our team",
      "description": "Athletic Trainer - University website My Profile Kiosk mode Join our team Athletic Trainer Athletic Trainer 492993 268 - Training Services Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time On-site $48,000 - $52,000 Add to favorites View favorites Overview Salem State University's Athletics program is built on the belief that student-athletes deserve the same quality of care and preparation as any competitor in the country. As a member of our sports medicine staff, you'll play a meaningful role in keeping that commitment — working directly with NCAA Division III student-athletes to support their health, performance, and long-term wellbeing. Reporting to the Assistant Athletic Director for Sports Medicine/Head Athletic Trainer, you will provide comprehensive athletic training services and assist in the implementation of a comprehensive sports medicine program to 15 varsity athletic teams. This is a hands-on, student-facing position with genuine scope to shape how care is delivered on campus and potentially serve as a preceptor for the MSAT program Please Note: This is a temporary, full-time, 10-month position with non-traditional hours including nights, weekends and travel with one high risk team. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree One year of collegiate athletic training experience or equivalent Current BOC Certification Possess or be eligible to acquire Massachusetts Athletic Trainer Licensure Professional Rescuer CPR/AED certification Preferred Qualifications Excellent communications skills; both written and oral Ability to successfully use and integrate MS Office or similar products in the working environment Ability to work a flexible schedule including nights and weekends Working Location This is an onsite position in Salem, MA with on-campus, in-person responsibilities, which may require regular work on evenings and weekends. Application Instructions Please apply online and attach resume and cover letter. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. This position is not eligible for H1B visa sponsorship. EEO Statement The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. ADA Statement Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. For accommodation information or requests please email eo-hr@salemstate.edu . Recruitment Agencies Salem State University does not partner with or accept candidates from outside staffing agencies. All hiring is managed directly by our internal Talent Acquisition team. Apply now First Name (required) e4d7a8c5 Last Name (required) 1aa9d326 Email (required) 8a3b4739 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Adjunct Faculty Day, Healthcare Studies, AY 2025-2026 493102 723 - Healthcare Studies Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Adjunct Faculty Evening - Continuing Education, English, AY 2026-2027 493089 163 - English Faculty: Adjunct, Staff: Temporary/Contract Part-Time Assistant Dean of Academic Advising 493046 256 - Ctr For Advising/Retention Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Faculty: History, (Early American and Public History), Full-Time, Temporary 493082 190 - History Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Non-Tenure-Track (Temp) Director of Academic Operations 493076 101 - Academic Affairs/ OVP Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Field Placement and First-Year Advising Coordinator 493038 234 - Psychology Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 95b68828 Last Name (required) 4ed310ff Email (required) 0bfef180 Job Alert 78b1f350 Finalize your job alert by selec