    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/faculty-childhood-education-and-care-special-education-full-time-temporary-spring-2027": {
      "title": "Join our team",
      "description": "Faculty: Childhood Education and Care, (Special Education), Full-Time, Temporary, Spring 2027 - University website My Profile Kiosk mode Join our team Faculty: Childhood Education and Care, (Special Education), Full-Time, Temporary, Spring 2027 Faculty: Childhood Education and Care, (Special Education), Full-Time, Temporary, Spring 2027 492982 443 - Childhood Education and Care Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Non-Tenure-Track (Temp) On-site $80,000 - $85,000 (for the rank of assistant professor) Add to favorites View favorites Overview Salem State University invites applications for a full-time, temporary faculty position in Special Education beginning in Spring 2027. The successful candidate will contribute to a dynamic educator preparation program committed to inclusive practices, equity, and strong partnerships with schools and communities. At Salem State University, academic excellence and student success are at the heart of our mission. As a public university, we are dedicated to providing an inclusive and supportive environment that fosters our students' learning and growth. We seek faculty who share our values of collegiality, civic engagement and continuous improvement. Join us in a community where your commitment to scholarship and teaching will empower students to make meaningful contributions to society. Duties and Responsibilities Candidates are required to perform duties in accordance with the MSCA contract . Duties include teaching, advising, scholarship and contributions to continuously improve the department and university. The standard teaching load is 12 credit hours per semester. The position is subject to available funding. Required Qualifications Earned doctoral degree in Special Education or a closely related field (by time of appointment). Professional experience as a Special Education teacher. Demonstrated commitment to inclusive instructional practices in educational settings and culturally responsive practices. A scholarly agenda Strong organizational and written and communication skills Expertise in one or more of the following areas: Evidence-based instructional practices, materials, and methods for teaching students with moderate disabilities Literacy instruction for students with disabilities Diagnostic and educational assessment for students with disabilities Development, interpretation, and implementation of Individualized Education Programs (IEPs) Autism spectrum disorder, including school-based and home-based interventions, collaboration with families, and advocacy for students with autism Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching in higher education. Experience with online asynchronous or hybrid instruction and learning management systems, such as Canvas. Working Location This is an on-site position in Salem, MA with on-campus, in-person responsibilities. Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. For accommodation information or requests please email eo-hr@salemstate.edu . Application Instructions Please apply online and attach CV, cover letter, and unofficial transcripts. Application review will commence in September. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. This position is not eligible for H1B visa sponsorship. EEO Statement The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Recruitment Agencies Salem State University does not partner with or accept candidates from outside staffing agencies. All hiring is managed directly by our internal Talent Acquisition team. Apply now First Name (required) 3a1954b6 Last Name (required) c760a185 Email (required) 8794c6e6 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Adjunct Faculty Day, Healthcare Studies, AY 2025-2026 493102 723 - Healthcare Studies Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Adjunct Faculty Evening - Continuing Education, English, AY 2026-2027 493089 163 - English Faculty: Adjunct, Staff: Temporary/Contract Part-Time Assistant Dean of Academic Advising 493046 256 - Ctr For Advising/Retention Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Faculty: History, (Early American and Public History), Full-Time, Temporary 493082 190 - History Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Non-Tenure-Track (Temp) Director of Academic Operations 493076 101 - Academic Affairs/ OVP Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Field Placement and First-Year Advising Coordinator 493038 234 - Psychology Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 3c57542d Last Name (required) d800987a Email (required) b4791222 Job Alert a034ee3f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 443 - Childhood Education and Care 443 - Childhood Education and Care Categories Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Employment Type Non-Tenure-Track (Temp) Non-Tenure-Track (Temp) Working location On-site On-site Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Apply Now First Name (required) 13edda27 Last Name (required) e3e8728e Email (required) 8e5a7808 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated u