    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/faculty-secondary-and-higher-education-school-counseling-full-time-professor-of-practice": {
      "title": "Faculty: Secondary and Higher Education (School Counseling), Full-Time, Professor of Practice -",
      "description": "Faculty: Secondary and Higher Education (School Counseling), Full-Time, Professor of Practice - University website My Profile Kiosk mode Join our team Faculty: Secondary and Higher Education (School Counseling), Full-Time, Professor of Practice Faculty: Secondary and Higher Education (School Counseling), Full-Time, Professor of Practice 492980 444 - Secondary and Higher Education Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Professor of Practice On-site $80,000 - $85,000 (for the rank of assistant professor) Add to favorites View favorites Overview The McKeown School of Education is seeking applicants for a full-time, professor of practice position with a specialization in School Counseling beginning in September 2027. The School Counseling Program prepares candidates to be educational leaders, social justice advocates, and system change agents with an emphasis on working in a variety of urban and suburban settings. This faculty member will teach a total of six graduate level classes per year, as well as advising school counseling students. Course topics may include: Multicultural Counseling, Career Counseling, Seminar in School Adjustment Counseling, and School Counseling practicum/seminar courses. Additional information about School Counseling Program can be found here: https://www.salemstate.edu/academics/mckeown-school-education/school-counseling/master-education-school-counseling Salem State University is a public institution with a clear sense of its mission: to provide an exceptional education that opens doors and transforms lives. As the Commonwealth's Civic Engagement University, we foster partnerships between our campus and the communities we serve, and our faculty are essential to that work. Our scholars and educators believe in what they do and thrive in a supportive, inclusive academic environment. As a proud Hispanic and Minority-Serving Institution, we're proud of the students we serve and the community we've built around their success. Join a university where your research, your teaching and your values all have room to flourish. Please Note: This is a four year, fixed term position ending on May 31, 2031 . Duties and Responsibilities Candidates are required to perform duties in accordance with the MSCA contract . Duties include teaching, advising, and demonstrated consistent and substantive effort to maintaining modern skills and knowledge in their field of practice. The standard teaching load is 12 credit hours per semester. The position is subject to available funding. This position will work collaboratively with the graduate program coordinator and the field office to facilitate program coordination. For the academic year 2027-2028, shared program coordination duties include: The direct supervision of school counseling candidates Conducting student admission reviews and new student onboarding Managing students’ plans of study Monitoring of internship and practicum site approval and accountability Reporting of hours Assisting with curriculum planning Maintaining records for a program with national reach. Required Qualifications An earned masters degree in school counseling or a related area Current licensure/certification as a practicing school counselor A minimum of three years of documented prior experience as a school counselor An understanding of the school adjustment counselor role Experience working with students through hybrid learning, mentoring, and training Membership in the American School Counseling Association Preferred Qualifications An earned PhD in Counselor Education from a CACREP-accredited program or PhD in Counseling Psychology from an APA-accredited program Evidence of strong clinical skills and a strong school counselor identity Evidence of strong teaching skills at the undergraduate and graduate levels Salem State University seeks faculty and librarians whose teaching, scholarship, and service will contribute to student success, academic excellence, and the university’s public mission. We welcome candidates with demonstrated ability to work effectively with students from varied backgrounds and to support an inclusive learning environment. Applicants may describe relevant accomplishments in teaching, scholarship/research, service, and community-engaged work Working Location This is an onsite position in Salem, MA with on-campus, in-person responsibilities. Application Instructions Please apply online and attach CV, cover letter, and unofficial transcripts. Application review will commence in September. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. This position is not eligible for H1B visa sponsorship. EEO Statement The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. ADA Statement Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. For accommodation information or requests please email eo-hr@salemstate.edu . Recruitment Agencies Salem State University does not partner with or accept candidates from outside staffing agencies. All hiring is managed directly by our internal Talent Acquisition team. Apply now First Name (required) e0b19777 Last Name (required) 7e0148fb Email (required) 220ba109 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Adjunct Faculty Day, Healthcare Studies, AY 2025-2026 493102 723 - Healthcare Studies Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Adjunct Faculty Evening - Continuing Education, English, AY 2026-2027 493089 163 - English Faculty: Adjunct, Staff: Temporary/Contract Part-Time Assistant Dean of Academic Advising 493046 256 - Ctr For Advising/Retention Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Faculty: History, (Early American and Public History), Full-Time, Temporary 493082 190 - History Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Non-Tenure-Track (Temp) Director of Academic Operations 493076 101 - Academic Affairs/ OVP Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Field Placement and First-Year Advising Coordinator 493038 234 - Psychology Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 8aacb2c8 Last Name (required) d2e472c8 Email (required) cd34da1c Job Alert 3d7d70b7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 444 - Secondary and Higher Education 444 - Secondary and Higher Education Categories Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Employment Type Professor of Practice Professor of Practice Working location On-site On-site Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Apply Now First Name (required) d47d7290 Last Name (required) f17d41cd Email (required) f4f3757e Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. You can view our university policies here . Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Technical and functional cookies are required for the Website to work. These include, for example, session management, Website security, shopping cart, language preferences, app launch, app management, or API (Application Program Interface) management. Perf