    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/faculty-childhood-education-and-care-literacy-full-time-professor-of-practice": {
      "title": "Faculty, Childhood Education and Care (Literacy), Full-Time, Professor of Practice -",
      "description": "Faculty, Childhood Education and Care (Literacy), Full-Time, Professor of Practice - University website My Profile Kiosk mode Join our team Faculty, Childhood Education and Care (Literacy), Full-Time, Professor of Practice Faculty, Childhood Education and Care (Literacy), Full-Time, Professor of Practice 492985 443 - Childhood Education and Care Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Professor of Practice On-site $80,000-$85,000 (for the rank of assistant professor) Add to favorites View favorites Overview The Professor of Practice, Literacy is a non-tenure track faculty position focused on strengthening literacy instruction and clinical practice within educator preparation programs at Salem State. In addition to teaching literacy courses, this role centers on supervising teacher candidates, training and coaching other supervisors, and ensuring high-quality practicum experiences are aligned with state standards, with a particular emphasis on literacy across Early Childhood, Elementary, and Moderate Disabilities (PK–8) licensure programs. This position begins in Fall 2027. Salem State University is where scholarship meets purpose. As the Commonwealth's Civic Engagement University, we believe education matters beyond the classroom, and our faculty are central to that mission. They bring intellectual curiosity and a genuine commitment to student success, teaching students who will go on to shape their communities, many of whom are the first in their families to earn a college degree. We value collaboration, academic rigor and the kind of civic-minded engagement that makes a real difference. If you're driven by meaningful work and want to be part of something bigger than any single course or semester, Salem State is your place. Please Note: This is a four year, fixed term position ending on May 31, 2031 . Duties and Responsibilities Candidates are required to perform duties in accordance with the MSCA contract . Duties include teaching, advising, and demonstrated consistent and substantive effort to maintaining modern skills and knowledge in their field of practice. The standard teaching load is 12 credit hours per semester. The position is subject to available funding. Specific Duties and Responsibilities Teach literacy related, DESE aligned education courses for teacher candidates in the Early Childhood, Elementary and Moderate Disabilities licensure programs. Supervise teacher candidates in practicum placements for Early Childhood, Elementary, and/or Moderate Disabilities (PK–8) licensure programs, with a focus on effective literacy instruction. Train, coach, support and provide feedback to practicum supervisors in observing and evaluating literacy instruction in alignment with Massachusetts Department of Elementary and Secondary Education (DESE) program approval expectations. Develop, deliver and evaluate professional learning for practicum supervisors to ensure consistency and quality in literacy-focused observation and feedback. Collaborate closely with the McKeown School of Education Office of Licensure and Field Engagement to support candidate success and the quality of pre-practicum and practicum placements aligned with DESE’s expectations for high quality instructional materials and evidence-based, culturally and linguistically sustaining literacy instruction. Collaborate with faculty in the McKeown School of Education on the content of literacy education courses. Support continuous program improvement efforts related to literacy and state approval standards. Maintain strong partnerships with schools and districts to support high-quality pre-practicum and practicum experiences. Required Qualifications Master’s degree or higher in Early Childhood Education, Elementary Education, Special Education, Literacy, or a closely related field. Reading Specialist license or PreK-2 or 1-6 Teacher license or Moderate Disabilities license (PreK-8) or a comparable license or an equivalent credential that demonstrates advanced literacy expertise. Significant professional experience (at least five years) teaching literacy. Demonstrated expertise in evidence-based literacy instruction and assessment. Experience mentoring, supervising, or coaching teacher candidates and/or practicing educators. Familiarity with Massachusetts DESE early literacy standards and program approval expectations. Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree in a relevant field. Prior experience training or supporting practicum supervisors or instructional coaches. Teaching experience in higher education and/or educator preparation programs. Strong collaboration and partnership-building skills with PK–12 schools and districts. Demonstrated technology skills, including the ability to use learning management systems, such as Canvas. Salem State University seeks faculty and librarians whose teaching, scholarship, and service will contribute to student success, academic excellence, and the university’s public mission. We welcome candidates with demonstrated ability to work effectively with students from varied backgrounds and to support an inclusive learning environment. Applicants may describe relevant accomplishments in teaching, scholarship/research, service, and community-engaged work. Working Location This is an onsite position in Salem, MA with on-campus, in-person responsibilities. Application Instructions Please apply online and attach CV, cover letter, and unofficial transcripts. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. This position is not eligible for H1B visa sponsorship. EEO Statement The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. ADA Statement Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. For accommodation information or requests please email eo-hr@salemstate.edu . Recruitment Agencies Salem State University does not partner with or accept candidates from outside staffing agencies. All hiring is managed directly by our internal Talent Acquisition team. Apply now First Name (required) c97396f0 Last Name (required) 2eaa8a86 Email (required) 93f8692d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Adjunct Faculty Day, Healthcare Studies, AY 2025-2026 493102 723 - Healthcare Studies Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Adjunct Faculty Evening - Continuing Education, English, AY 2026-2027 493089 163 - English Faculty: Adjunct, Staff: Temporary/Contract Part-Time Assistant Dean of Academic Advising 493046 256 - Ctr For Advising/Retention Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Faculty: History, (Early American and Public History), Full-Time, Temporary 493082 190 - History Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Non-Tenure-Track (Temp) Director of Academic Operations 493076 101 - Academic Affairs/ OVP Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Field Placement and First-Year Advising Coordinator 493038 234 - Psychology Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) a09f759b Last Name (required) 8c03c076 Email (required) 735d1836 Job Alert df44cead Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 443 - Childhood Education and Care 443 - Childhood Education and Care Categories Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Employment Type Professor of Practice Professor of Practice Working location On-site On-site Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Apply 