    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/faculty-geography-geospatial-ai-full-time-temporary": {
      "title": "Join our team",
      "description": "Faculty: Geography, (Geospatial AI), Full-Time, Temporary - University website My Profile Kiosk mode Join our team Faculty: Geography, (Geospatial AI), Full-Time, Temporary Faculty: Geography, (Geospatial AI), Full-Time, Temporary 492991 181 - Geography Department Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Non-Tenure-Track (Temp) On-site $90,000-$95,000 (for the rank of assistant professor) Add to favorites View favorites Overview We seek a collaborative scholar with expertise in GeoAI (Geospatial Artificial Intelligence) to study climate science (meteorology, weather forecasting and prediction, extreme events, climate change and climate change modeling, etc.), climate resilience, and spatial data science to address pressing socio-environmental challenges for a temporary, full-time role beginning in Fall 2027. The successful candidate will demonstrate expertise in GeoAI and climate science with track record of working across disciplines on climate adaptation, environmental justice, and sustainability. Salem State University is a place where academic excellence and a dedication to teaching come together. We embrace the uniqueness of our faculty, creating a collegial and collaborative environment where you can excel in your scholarly and teaching pursuits. Our commitment to civic engagement and the success of our students drives our work. We seek faculty who value continuous improvement and accountability. Join us and be part of a vibrant academic community that transforms lives and enriches the Commonwealth. Duties and Responsibilities Candidates are required to perform duties in accordance with the MSCA contract . Duties include teaching, advising, scholarship and contributions to continuously improve the department and university. The standard teaching load is 12 credit hours per semester. The position is subject to available funding. Depending on the student enrollment trends and the department needs, it is possible, but not guaranteed, to renew the temporary full time position in future academic years. Required Qualifications PhD in Geography or related field. Demonstrated experience teaching undergraduate weather and climate courses or closely related physical geography courses. Demonstrated experience applying machine learning or AI methods to environmental, climate, or geospatial datasets. Preferred Qualifications Ability to develop an undergraduate GeoAI course to support majors and minors entering the workforce. Experience mentoring students in applied geospatial research and/or utilizing it professional settings. Salem State University seeks faculty and librarians whose teaching, scholarship, and service will contribute to student success, academic excellence, and the university’s public mission. We welcome candidates with demonstrated ability to work effectively with students from varied backgrounds and to support an inclusive learning environment. Applicants may describe relevant accomplishments in teaching, scholarship/research, service, and community-engaged work. Working Location This is an onsite position in Salem, MA with on-campus, in-person responsibilities. Application Instructions Please apply online and attach CV, cover letter, and unofficial transcripts. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. This position is not eligible for H1B visa sponsorship. EEO Statement The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. ADA Statement Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. For accommodation information or requests please email eo-hr@salemstate.edu . Recruitment Agencies Salem State University does not partner with or accept candidates from outside staffing agencies. All hiring is managed directly by our internal Talent Acquisition team. Apply now First Name (required) 89158f59 Last Name (required) 5f5c720e Email (required) 1293b9ea Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Adjunct Faculty Day, Healthcare Studies, AY 2025-2026 493102 723 - Healthcare Studies Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Adjunct Faculty Evening - Continuing Education, English, AY 2026-2027 493089 163 - English Faculty: Adjunct, Staff: Temporary/Contract Part-Time Assistant Dean of Academic Advising 493046 256 - Ctr For Advising/Retention Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Faculty: History, (Early American and Public History), Full-Time, Temporary 493082 190 - History Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Non-Tenure-Track (Temp) Director of Academic Operations 493076 101 - Academic Affairs/ OVP Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Field Placement and First-Year Advising Coordinator 493038 234 - Psychology Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 39b64336 Last Name (required) f29a56cb Email (required) 6dee5474 Job Alert f7680253 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 181 - Geography Department 181 - Geography Department Categories Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Employment Type Non-Tenure-Track (Temp) Non-Tenure-Track (Temp) Working location On-site On-site Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Apply Now First Name (required) 8700e094 Last Name (required) 7e87348b Email (required) 6c7a470e Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to p